<PageLayout title="Troubleshooting Guide & Solutions — TotalRecalls" description="Step-by-step troubleshooting guide for TotalRecalls: fixing login hurdles, download retries, Takeout imports, and license activation issues." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }, { label: "Troubleshooting" }]}>
  <h1>Troubleshooting Guide</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    TotalRecalls is engineered to be resilient across eight different AI vendor platforms. When an unexpected
    connection pause or download interrupt occurs, consult the proven recovery steps below.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Provider Sign-In Window Closes or Returns Empty</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Embedded Window vs. Default Browser:</strong> TotalRecalls uses an isolated, secure embedded Chromium
      runtime on your machine to capture session tokens. Sign in directly inside that window — the app does not and
      cannot read cookies or passwords from your default Chrome, Edge, or Firefox browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare Verification Challenges:</strong> Providers like Perplexity and Claude often present
      Cloudflare Turnstile or CAPTCHA verification challenges during sign-in. If a challenge appears, complete it
      interactively inside the window and wait 3–5 seconds until the provider dashboard renders before closing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Blank Window on Launch:</strong> If the login window opens blank or fails to render, close TotalRecalls
      and reopen it. The app automatically scans for and terminates orphaned background browser instances on startup.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Forcing a Fresh Session:</strong> Click <em>Disconnect</em> next to the provider name in the app, then
      click <em>Connect</em> again to purge expired cached cookies and launch a fresh sign-in dialog.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. "Servers Are Busy — Retrying" During Large Exports</h2>
  <p>
    When extracting hundreds or thousands of historical conversations, provider APIs (notably ChatGPT and Perplexity)
    occasionally issue HTTP 429 rate-limit warnings or 503 gateway timeouts.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Automatic Exponential Backoff:</strong> Do not abort the run. TotalRecalls features an automatic retry
      queue with intelligent backoff pacing. The app will hold your progress, wait for the provider's cooldown window
      to clear, and resume smoothly from the exact last saved conversation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Incremental Refresh:</strong> If you stop an export early, running it again will not redownload existing
      conversations. The app compares remote timestamps against your local metadata manifest and downloads only new
      or modified conversations.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Google Takeout Gemini Import Hurdles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Extract the Archive First:</strong> TotalRecalls reads uncompressed directory structures. If you import
      directly from <code>takeout-2026.zip</code>, the file picker cannot parse the contents. Right-click the ZIP in
      Windows Explorer, select <em>Extract All</em>, and point TotalRecalls to the extracted folder.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Nested Takeout Folder Hierarchy:</strong> Select either the root <code>Takeout\</code> folder or the
      nested <code>Takeout\Gemini\</code> (or <code>Takeout\Bard\</code>) directory. TotalRecalls recursively traverses
      all subdirectories to locate your JSON and HTML chat dumps.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. License Activation Key Errors</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Key Format:</strong> Pro license keys follow the format <code>TR-XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX</code>. Smart Search
      Engine keys follow <code>SSE-XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX</code>. Ensure you enter your Downloader key into the Downloader app.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Clipboard Whitespace:</strong> When pasting your key from email, ensure no trailing spaces or newline
      characters were copied before clicking <em>Activate</em>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>One-Time Internet Connection:</strong> License activation requires an active internet connection to
      communicate with our secure verification endpoint once. Once activated, the app operates 100% offline.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Smart Search Engine (SSE) First-Run Indexing Notice</h2>
  <p>
    When launching the Smart Search Engine add-on for the first time across a large library (1,000+ conversations),
    local vectorization and embedding generation runs entirely on your local CPU. This initial process takes between
    <strong>5 to 15 minutes</strong> depending on your processor. Do not close the terminal window while the progress
    bar advances; subsequent searches launch instantly.
  </p>

  <h2>Still Need Assistance?</h2>
  <p>
    Our engineering team is available directly at <a href="mailto:support@totalrecalls.app">support@totalrecalls.app</a>.
    Include your Windows version and provider name for priority diagnostic assistance.
  </p>
